    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101325" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σύρτις</span></b> , gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιος</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			D.P.
			477
		</span></i>, ἡ: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύρω</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the Syrtis</i>, name of two large shallow gulfs on the
			coast of Libya, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				150
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			metaph., <i>destruction</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλα δ᾽
				ἄλλαν θραῦεν ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Tim.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				99
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Orat.</u>
				3.41.163
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
